     "rationale": "A09 Curtain walling and cladding currently waits for the whole of A06 (decking and upper floor slabs) to finish before it can start, even though the facade can follow the frame floor by floor once steel erection is complete. Letting A09 start as soon as A05 finishes lets the glazing crew mobilise on the lower floors while decking and slab pours continue above, recovering time on the critical path with no extra labour or cost.",
     "risks": "Steel erectors and glazing installers will be working on the structure at the same time, so crane time, access and temporary edge protection need careful coordination. Temporary works and CDM sign-off for concurrent trades must be reviewed before site adopts this sequence.",
