     "rationale": "A05 Structural steel frame erection is the activity immediately affected by the late steel delivery and sits on the critical path. Labour-driven erection work can typically be compressed by up to 30% with an extra erection gang and weekend working, clawing back days lost to the delayed delivery of PO-24110.",
     "risks": "Specialist steel erectors are hard to source at short notice; extra crane hire and possible out-of-hours consent may be needed. Erection is also wind-sensitive, so weekend lifts could be lost to weather. Cost is a variation unless recoverable from the steel supplier.",
